# Switching HT
For lower kV, a shorting jig needs to be inserted to ensure the brightness of the source is high because that will retain the same voltage per HT plate. This jig can only be inserted when HT is off. So, directly switching from 200kV to 80kV will not insert jig.

Instead, we go to 0kV, insert jig, and then go up to 80kV. The following picture shows the jig is not inserted (the copper is visible). When jig is inserted, you can no longer see copper. 